    "created_at": "2016-07-14T17:29:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-14T17:29:03Z",
    "body": "I'm curious what exactly is the \"in parallel\" work in each of these cases. If we make too much parallel, there seem to be possible race conditions. It seems like you need to do, in general, something like:\n- Copy data (or SVG text content??)\n- Return the promise\n- Go \"in parallel\"\n- Possibly decode, rasterize, and transform\n- Resolve (or reject) the promise\n\nIn many cases currently the copying step is mixed together with some other steps, e.g. \n\n> Let the ImageBitmap object's bitmap data be a copy of the canvas element's bitmap data, cropped to the source rectangle with formatting.\n\nAlso as noted in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/1547, \"rasterization\" for vector graphics is not as of now an explicit step.\n",
